{number: 21}
{title: I’ve Found a Friend, oh, Such a Friend}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I've found a Friend, oh, [F] such a Friend!
He [C] loved me ere I [G] knew Him;
He [C] drew me with the [F] cords of love,
And [C] thus He bound me [G7] to [C] Him.
And [G] round my heart still [C] closely twine
Those [F] ties which naught can [G] sever,
For [C] I am His, and [F] He is mine,
For-[C] ever and for-[G7] ev-[C] er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] I've found a Friend, oh, [F] such a Friend!
He [C] bled, He died to [G] save me;
And [C] not alone the [F] gift of life,
But [C] His own self He [G7] gave [C] me.
Naught [G] that I have my [C] own I'll call,
I'll [F] hold it for the [G] Giver;
My [C] heart, my strength, my [F] life, my all,
Are [C] His, and His for-[G7] ev-[C] er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] I've found a Friend, oh, [F] such a Friend!
All [C] power to Him is [G] given,
To [C] guard me on my [F] onward course,
And [C] bring me safe to [G7] hea-[C] ven.
The [G] eternal God is [C] my refuge,
And [F] underneath are [G] ever
The [C] everlasting [F] arms of love:
His [C] arms that fail me [G7] nev-[C] er.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] I've found a Friend, oh, [F] such a Friend!
So [C] kind, and true, and [G] tender,
So [C] wise a Counselor [F] and Guide,
So [C] mighty a De-[G7] fen-[C] der!
From [G] Him, Who loves me [C] now so well,
What [F] power my soul can [G] sever?
Shall [C] life or death, or [F] earth or hell?
No; [C] I am His for-[G7] ev-[C] er.
{end_of_verse}
